  "about": "Telemetry frames exactly as src/Protocol.cpp writes them, every key and no other: test/test_protocol builds the status each frame describes and checks that writeTelemetry() writes this frame back. The panel's tests read them through extras/joystick/test/firmware.js: panel.test.js checks what the page shows for each, and it and sim.test.js build their other frames from \"sweeping\". 999 is a bearing with no echo (DISTANCE_FAR_CM). \"firmware\" is the running image's MD5; these are made up. \"sonar\" is always sent, \"aim\" while it aims, \"aimCm\" once a reading at that angle is in, \"check\" while the checks run (\"move\" is STOP while one wheel turns alone, as in \"checking\"), and \"pad\" only by a build with the gamepad.",
